I did not know dwish was giving precision matrix and not covariance matrix.
As an output of my model I want a correlation matrix (based on the precision matrix). So if I understood well how it works (sorry it is the first time I meet precision matrices), I should tranform it into covariance matrix then correlation matrix as follow ?

code <- nimbleCode( {
        Omega[1:M,1:M] ~ dwish(R[1:M,1:M], 4)
        for(i in 1:N) {
            Y[i, 1:M] ~ dmnorm(mu[1:M], prec = Omega[1:M,1:M])
        }

        covar<-solve(Omega)

        for (i in 1:n_species){
              for (j in 1:n_species){

                    corr[i,j]<-covar[i,j]/sqrt(covar[i,i]*covar[j,j])
              }
         }

    })

